corbin-breton/repo-guardian  1.3.0 -> 1.3.1
change_type: instructions+code   changelog: repo-guardian 1.3.1  - Added support for configuring Reviewer A and Reviewer B agents via new environment variables (`GUARDIAN_AGENT` and `GUARDIAN_REVIEWER_B_AGENT`). - Updated documentation to clarify agent configuration and default selection for cross-model review. - Cron job documentation now uses a generic `<your-agent-name>` placeholder for improved clarity.

### SKILL.md  [instructions]
- version: 1.3.0
-     "agent": "keats",
+ version: 1.3.1
+     "agent": "<your-agent-name>",
+ - `GUARDIAN_AGENT` — OpenClaw agent name for Reviewer A (default: `$OPENCLAW_AGENT` or `default`)
+ - `GUARDIAN_REVIEWER_B_AGENT` — OpenClaw agent name for Reviewer B (default: same as `GUARDIAN_AGENT`; set to a different agent for true cross-model review)

### scripts/guardian.sh  [code]
-       OPUS_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent keats --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \
-       GPT_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent openforge-cloud --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \
-         GPT_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent openforge-cloud-fallback --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \
+ AGENT_NAME="${GUARDIAN_AGENT:-${OPENCLAW_AGENT:-default}}"
+ REVIEWER_B_AGENT="${GUARDIAN_REVIEWER_B_AGENT:-$AGENT_NAME}"
+       OPUS_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent "$AGENT_NAME" --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \
+       GPT_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent "$REVIEWER_B_AGENT" --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \
+         GPT_RESULT=$(openclaw agent --agent "$REVIEWER_B_AGENT" --local --message "$REVIEW_PROMPT" --json 2>/dev/null | \